{"user": "Im thinking about g2, but I am not too sure what the outcome of that would be", "user_ts": "2026-08-18T22:38:59.029834+00:00", "assistant": "If you play **g2**, Black flips **f2, f3, e4, d5** \u2014 so it looks good immediately.\n\nBut the key endgame question is: **what does White get next?** After **g2**, White seems to have replies like **a3** or **b6**. Also, **g2 is the X-square next to the h1 corner**, so check whether your move could eventually help White access **h1**.\n\nQuick test: after your imagined **g2**, ask:  \n1. Can White take a corner soon?  \n2. Does White have many moves, or are they restricted?  \n3. After White\u2019s best reply, are your remaining moves safe?", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-18T22:39:20.791111+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-18T22:39:23.003790+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Common Ground Question": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "votes": {"Board Report": 2, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 2, "Prompt": 3, "Move Verdict": 1, "Hint": 2}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 0.6666666666666666, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 0.6666666666666666, "Prompt": 1.0, "Move Verdict": 0.3333333333333333, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Bo