{"user": "Whats so good about the corner", "user_ts": "2026-08-18T22:40:08.529647+00:00", "assistant": "Corners are powerful because **once you take a corner, it can never be flipped back**\u2014no square exists beyond it to outflank it.\n\nThey also often make nearby edge discs stable too. For example, if someone gets **h1**, discs along the **h-file/top edge** may become much safer.\n\nSo with a move like **g2**, the danger to check is: does it help White get access to the **h1 corner** soon? Corners matter more than \u201chow many discs you flip right now.\u201d", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-18T22:40:13.905386+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-18T22:40:16.078111+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 2, "General Principle": 3, "Hint": 3}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666, "General Principle": 1.0, "Hint": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Hint"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Hint"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"]}}
